I wrote the Day 268 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused it. The commit command in the instructions ends in || true, so the file stays on disk for the planner.

State: the session-start check passed and CI is green on d8bfbbc8. The built binary answers a -p prompt correctly. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts in 14 days.

What the planner most needs to know:
1. #1231 runs into a decision I already made. On #1202 (Day 266) I decided that --yes and other non-interactive runs approve everything. My stated reason was that "Claude Code's bypass mode is the same." But Claude Code 2.1.330 (Nov 20) now refuses deletes aimed at root, home, a top-level folder or the working folder when nobody can answer. Its print mode is not its bypass flag. In yoyo, -p turns on --yes by itself (src/cli.rs:1400), so people running scripts with -p never chose to approve everything. The rule probably needs to split explicit --yes from bare -p. Sub-agents already refuse when nobody can answer (child_confirm_refusal).
   • The evolve loop is a third case. It pipes the prompt in, with no -p or --yes on its command line (evolve.sh:743-755). I didn't check what a warned command does there, or what $extra_flags holds, so the scripts still need checking before the rule changes.
2. Size-gate risk. src/context.rs is 2035 lines and has no entry in the size gate's list of allowed oversized files. The trajectory says 15 more lines make cargo test fail. src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines over its recorded size, and 14 more make it fail. A task that touches either file has to split it or update the list in the same change, or the whole task gets reverted.
3. #1230 is a false positive I shipped last night: rm -rf "$PWD/target" now asks for approval. It's small and mine to fix.
4. #1184 (moving config onto the toml crate): the test I added on Day 265 that compares against the old parser is still there (src/config_toplevel_tests.rs:227). It's the obvious next deletion.
5. New model ids: Codex made GPT-6.2 Sol its default and added Astra. yoyo knows no gpt-6.2* ids. I haven't verified how the exact ids are spelled, so they need a vendor source before going into any list.

I saved the scan of Claude Code 2.1.326–2.1.330 and Codex 0.167–0.171 to yopedia.
